											<item_modify>
												<item type="scrap" min="120" max="120"/>
											</item_modify>
										</event>
									</choice>
									
									<choice req="DJMOD_LASER_BPS" hidden="true">
										<text>Sell them your BPS Messenger laser for 200~.</text>
										<event>
											<text>You try to hide your satisfaction while they transfer the excessive payment, but also hope some unfortunate encounter won't make you regret the sale in the near future.</text>
											<remove name="DJMOD_LASER_BPS"/>
											<item_modify>
												<item type="scrap" min="200" max="200"/>
											</item_modify>
										</event>
									</choice>
									
									<choice>
										<text>Decline.</text>
										<event>
											<text>You think about the profit you could have made from this encounter, but also remember that selling your weapons to random passerbys isn't a very safe strategy.
												You still have time to do something around the ship instead.
											</text>
											
											<choice>
												<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
												<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
											</choice>
											<choice>
												<text>Do nothing.</text>
												<event/>
											</choice>
										</event>
									</choice>
								</event>
							</choice>
							
							<choice req="DJMOD_HAS_RADIKAL_GEAR">
								<text>(RadiKal gear) Power up your weapons before they take YOUR equipment by force.</text>
								<event>
									<text>"Alright alright, no need to resort to violence. We'll be on our way."</text>
									
									<choice hidden="true">
										<text>...Well that means they're as weak as they said, let's make some easy scrap!</text>
										<event>
											<text>"Wait... Wait! Thi-this was just a trade request. How did it come to this? Please!"
											As you suspected from the covert nature of their mission, they're not sending any message to denounce you, merely firing up their engines to escape! Looks like you've found a place where crime can go unpunished...</text>
											<ship hostile="true"/>
											<choice hidden="true">
												<text>Continue...</text>
												<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
											</choice>
										</event>
									</choice>
									
									<choice hidden="true">
										<text>Leave them be, they are clearly no threat.</text>
										<event/>
									</choice>
								</event>
							</choice>
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>

			<choice req="DJMOD_HAS_RADIKAL_SHIP" hidden="true">
				<text>That's funny. How did you get here without ever seeing an RK ship?</text>
				<event>
					<text>What? Wait how would you know that?.. Oh I see, this must in fact be a RadiKal ship! Can we... have it? We will compensate you greatly.</text>

					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Hmmmmm, no.</text>
						<event>
							<text>"Figured as much... but understand that my whole family died to a RadiKal raid while I was on duty. I didn't take this assignment at random. We need access to hinder their operations, and I really can't let that opportunity pass. I wish you had cooperated, it pains me to do this but I must!"

							Their weapons are coming online!</text>
							<ship hostile="true"/>

							<choice hidden="true">
								<text>Continue...</text>
								<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
							</choice>
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Ignore them.</text>
		<event>
			<text>You leave them to whatever troubles they're having, and think about doing some maintenance on your ship instead.</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
				<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Do nothing.</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>
<ship name="SHIP_RK_GEAR_BUYER_ZOLTAN" auto_blueprint="MU_ZOLTAN_TRANSPORT">
	<!-- If you do not include a chance, then it will always attempt to surrender. -->
	<surrender chance="0.9" min="2" max="5" load="SURRENDER_ZOLTAN"/>
	<escape timer="30" min="999" max="999"/>
	<gotaway load="RK_GEAR_BUYER_ZOLTAN_GOTAWAY"/>
	<destroyed load="DESTROYED_ZOLTAN"/>
	<deadCrew load="DEAD_CREW_ZOLTAN"/>
	<weaponOverride count="1">
		<name>LIST_WEAPONS_ZOLTAN</name>
	</weaponOverride>
</ship>
<event name="RK_GEAR_BUYER_ZOLTAN_GOTAWAY">
	<text>The Zoltans escape before you can slaughter them for scrap, and contrary to what you thought, actually do denounce you. Fair enough.</text>		
	<choice>
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<!-- <event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ZOLTAN_FIGHT"/> 	This one leads to COMBAT_CHECK -->
		<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ZOLTAN"/>
	</choice>
</event>


<!-- Granny on planet or "nearby station" (no sprite?) describes the 3 RadiKal subfactions if you wait. Reward for fleetboost. -->
<FTL>
<event name="RADIKAL_PHILO">
	<preventQuest/>
	<text>You find a welcoming, lively senior hermit in a small space station chock-full of civilian and military supplies, apparently all for herself. 
		"Hello foreigner, I know all about this sector, care to listen and have some tea?"</text>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Stay for a while. This could be helpful.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Name's Bruntilda. As you've certainly noticed, this sector is occupied by three main subfactions, and they all have their own personality!"</text>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Politely interrupt and ask where those supplies came from.</text>
				<event>
					<text>"Oh, aren't you curious! You see my dear, my sons work in this sector in "management" and "marketing" positions. At one point they realized they didn't have the time or patience to assess newcomers and teach them our ways. So they came up with this gig for their sweet ol' mama, and they're always making sure I am cared for."</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>I see. Nice to meet you.</text>
						<event>
							<text>Now that you can guess why nobody's pillaged the place yet, there are things you could learn about. "What else would you like to know, dear?"</text>
							<choice hidden="true">
								<text>Think of some questions.</text>
								<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
							</choice>
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>We don't have time to waste with some grandma's "intel".</text>
		<event>
			<text>You say goodbye, gaining and losing nothing, which isn't that bad when you think about it.</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
				<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Do nothing.</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>
<event name="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD">
	<loadEvent>RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_REAL</loadEvent>
	
	<!-- This can help enforce randomness. probably not useful here but good reference. -->
	<!-- <loadEvent seeded="false">RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_REAL</loadEvent> -->
</event>
<event name="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_REAL">
	<text>Ask her...</text>

	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>... about the Gatekeepers.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"This is supposed to be a bit of a surprise, but I've met some charming lads and lassies who never made it out of the sector because they didn't know. So I'll tell you: you're not leaving the sector without a fight (unless you're transporting one of our friends, hah!). Steer clear until you're prepared.
				
				The Bam gatekeeper will be a tough nut to crack, but any missile defense and sufficient shielding should keep you safe.

				The Punk gatekeeper has a bit of a chaotic mess going on, but it's mostly ion and anti-bio damage you must watch out for.

				The Scorch gatekeeper will have you on fire soon and repeatedly, and that won't work too well against it either. But surely you already figured that one out!
				
				Just don't let my sons know I told you all that, Heeeheeehee! Oh and you can always just run away if you're a pussycat..."
				You can tell that even she would no longer respect you if you did that, but you must also think about the reality you're trying to save.
				</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Ask her something else.</text>
				<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Leave.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You grab your things.</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
						<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>... about the subfaction names.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"What kind of names are those? RadiKal Bam? Punk? Scorch? Is it from a kid's show or something?" you ask.
			
			"Not much to it really. Since so many people have been calling them radicals from the beginning of this little operation, my sons and their little friends simply embraced it. The subfactions just needed a little extra to tell themselves apart, and people don't really like talking too much around here. So they kept it short and to the point. Also I've heard something about variables? I'm the exception, chatting is so enjoyable!"
			</text>
						
			<choice>
				<text>Ask her something else.</text>
				<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Leave.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You grab your things.</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
						<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>... about the RK equipment design philosophy.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Maybe you're just a little slow in the head, so just in case, let me lay it out for youuu." You repress the urge to respond to the insult.
			
			"Members of Bam believe in the blunt efficiency of impactful, stunning hits or events. Such as a good bonk to the dome, like I taught my children!
		
			The Punk prefer technological superiority, counter-intelligence and all that jazz. They tend to bring less firepower and more fancy gadgets to the table.
		
			Lastly the Scorch just want to watch things burn, and have ways to make sure they do. Some jealous foreigners like to spout nonsense about pacts with otherwordly creatures, especially among the Scorch. Isn't it sad, how low people will go?
		
			I hope that clears it up for y'all youngsters!"</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Ask her something else.</text>
				<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Leave.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You grab your things.</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
						<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>... about the prices.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"It takes a lot of specialized equipment to discreetly get so many crafting materials into a hidden sector, or so my sons told me. That leads to high prices, but not so much for the local production of course!"</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Ask her something else.</text>
				<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Leave.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You grab your things.</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
						<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<!-- <choice hidden="true">
		<text>... about the contests.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"The inevitable but usually friendly rivalry between the factions leads to many confrontations to figure out whose equipment is the best. 
				Even tourists like you can partake, so long as they own a piece. Sometimes they even survive!"</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Ask her something else.</text>
				<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_INTEL_LOAD"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Leave.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You grab your things.</text>
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
						<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice> -->
	
	<choice req="pilot" lvl="1" hidden="true" blue="false" max_group="2">
		<text>Threaten her for the supplies!</text>
		<event>
			<text>Emboldened by her physical frailty, you decide chatting is never gonna be as useful as just taking what you want.</text>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>How about you just shut up and give us all of those suppl-</text>
				<event>
					<text>Before you can finish your despicable threat, you feel the cold dagger belonging to a cloaked security drone pressing on your neck, and realize this whole place is obviously heavily defended.
					"Uneducated scallywags, eh? Another disappointment, but it is clear that our little business is attractive to this type of people. What a waste of good tea. Out with you now."</text>
					
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Wait a sec! You won't believe it but, this really isn't who we are...</text>
						<event>
							<text>You shamefully "offer" some supplies as an apology, find out why the pile is so big, and tell your crew in very clear terms that this event is not to be talked about ever again.
							You also feel like even though this happened in this hidden sector, word of your lack of morals could somehow reach the outside world.</text>

							<item_modify steal="true">
								<item type="scrap" min="-20" max="-10"/>
								<item type="missiles" min="-5" max="-3"/>
								<item type="drones" min="-3" max="-2"/>
							</item_modify>
							<event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_GENERAL"/>		<!-- does nothing? try in a choice wrapper -->
							<!-- <event/> -->
						</event>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice req="pilot" lvl="1" hidden="true" blue="false" max_group="3">
		<text>Alright, we'll be on our way now. Thank you for the tea.</text>
		<event load="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE"/>
	</choice>
</event>
<event name="RADIKAL_PHILO_GOODBYE">
	<text>She looks cheerful. "Why, thank you! Very few of you young'uns take a pause to listen to an old lady around these parts. For some reason they seem to favor... 'enhanced interrogation' I think the kids call it? Something about manufacturing details. Anyhoo, farewell!"
	You notice a shuttle sent to share a little of her supplies with you. That job might be lonelier than it looks, and you wonder how often her sons visit her.</text>
	<autoReward level="HIGH">stuff</autoReward>
	<modifyPursuit amount="1"/>
	
	<choice>
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event/>
	</choice>
</event>
</FTL>

<!-- QUEST SPAWNER - Anti-RadiKals police checking and fining for illegal gear, possibly seizing it, temporarily or not. 
About 900 lines, minimize if not interested. -->
<FTL>
<event name="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK">
	<preventQuest/>
	<!-- <customFleet right="false" firing="true" autoDarkening="true">CUSTOM_FLEET_ENGINEER</customFleet> 	CRASH! on sector jump -->
	<!-- <customFleet right="false" firing="false" autoDarkening="true">CUSTOM_FLEET_ZOLTAN</customFleet> 	CRASH! on sector jump -->
	<text>As soon as you get here, you notice that you're surrounded by a small Zoltan fleet intercepting every ship passing through here. An urgent hail from a heavily armed Zoltan Elite comes through. 
		Needless to say, it would look suspicious not to take the hail.
	</text>
	<ship load="SHIP_RKS_ZOLTAN_POLICE" hostile="false"/>
	<!-- <customFleet right="false" firing="false" autoDarkening="true">CUSTOM_FLEET_ZOLTAN</customFleet> 	Also CRASH below <text> -->
	<!-- <customFleet right="false" firing="true" autoDarkening="true">CUSTOM_FLEET_ENGINEER</customFleet> 	Also CRASH below <text> -->
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Answer it.</text>
		<event name="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_MENU">
			<text>"As you may know if you're not a brainless savage, this sector has been providing armament to the Duskbringers. We have recently started tackling this problem.
				Like any vessel in transit in a lawless armament-manufacturing area like this one, you will be subjected to the mandatory thorough search for said armament.
				
				The fight against illegal weapon proliferation starts with you. Do not resist."
				
				The Zoltan Ministry considers this area a very serious issue. If they find any RadiKal equipment a fine must be paid, based on how many you're carrying.
			</text>

			<choice req="zoltan_peacekeeper" hidden="true">
				<text>(Zoltan Peacekeeper) The Ministry sent us.</text>
				<event>
					<text>"At last, the reinforcements. Here is your warrant. You'll find criminals in this sector, usually hiding in hazardous beacons. Seize their illegal gear and drop it off at the station. The coordinates are on the back."
						
						It's safe to assume that not every "criminal" will relinquish their RK gear without a fight, but this could greatly benefit your mission.</text>

					<augment name="RKS_POLICE_WARRANT"/>
					
					<choice>
						<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
						<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
					</choice>
					<choice>
						<text>Do nothing.</text>
						<event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			<choice req="human_soldier" hidden="true">
				<text>(Human Soldier) The Federation sends their help.</text>
				<event>
					<text>"At last, the reinforcements. Here is your warrant. You'll find criminals in this sector, usually hiding in hazardous beacons. Seize their illegal gear and drop it off at the station. The coordinates are on the back."
						
						It's safe to assume that not every "criminal" will relinquish their RK gear without a fight, but this could greatly benefit your mission.</text>

					<augment name="RKS_POLICE_WARRANT"/>
					
					<choice>
						<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
						<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
					</choice>
					<choice>
						<text>Do nothing.</text>
						<event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			<choice req="engi_defender" hidden="true">
				<text>(Engi Defender) For the Harmony's prosperity, let us help.</text>
				<event>
					<text>"At last, the reinforcements. Here is your warrant. You'll find criminals in this sector, usually hiding in hazardous beacons. Seize their illegal gear and drop it off at the station. The coordinates are on the back."
						
						It's safe to assume that not every "criminal" will relinquish their RK gear without a fight, but this could greatly benefit your mission.</text>

					<augment name="RKS_POLICE_WARRANT"/>
					
					<choice>
						<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
						<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
					</choice>
					<choice>
						<text>Do nothing.</text>
						<event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			<choice req="orchid_praetor" hidden="true">
				<text>(Orchid Praetor) Gesture "We come to help".</text>
				<event>
					<text>"At last, the reinforcements. Here is your warrant. You'll find criminals in this sector, usually hiding in hazardous beacons. Seize their illegal gear and drop it off at the station. The coordinates are on the back."
						
						It's safe to assume that not every "criminal" will relinquish their RK gear without a fight, but this could greatly benefit your mission.</text>

					<augment name="RKS_POLICE_WARRANT"/>
					
					<choice>
						<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
						<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
					</choice>
					<choice>
						<text>Do nothing.</text>
						<event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Agree to the search.</text>
				<event load="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_ACCEPT"/>
			</choice>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Ask what happens if you refuse.</text>
				<event>
					<text>"Thanks to the merciful recent amendment 3473-B delta, captains may choose to participate in the funding of control vessels like this one, and report to the closest Zoltan police station within 72 cycles instead of immediately submitting to the search."
						Even though you have no intention of taking that detour, they would leave you alone for now.</text>
					
					<choice>
						<text>Pay up.</text>
						<event>
							<text>You begrudgingly transfer the scrap but manage to not look mad about it, taking comfort in the fact that your equipment's safe... at least for now.</text>
							<item_modify>
								<item type="scrap" min="-25" max="-25"/>
							</item_modify>
						</event>
					</choice>
					
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Agree to the search.</text>
						<event load="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_ACCEPT"/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Try to ignore it and just pass through.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Your admission of guilt in facilitating terrorist operations has been recorded and filed for the trial of any surviving spouse(s) and/or heir(s). You will not escape the law."
				Sounds like you'll have to fight your way through. You wonder whether having an insider in your crew could have changed this outcome.</text>
			<ship hostile="true"/>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<!-- <event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ZOLTAN_FIGHT"/> -->
				<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
		
</event>
<!-- <ship name="SHIP_RKS_ZOLTAN_POLICE" auto_blueprint="LIST_SHIPS_ZOLTAN_ELITE_GENERIC"> -->
<ship name="SHIP_RKS_ZOLTAN_POLICE" auto_blueprint="RKS_ZOLTAN_POLICE">
	<destroyed load="DEFEAT_ZOLTAN_ELITE"/>
	<deadCrew load="DEFEAT_ZOLTAN_ELITE"/>
	<!-- THIS CRASHES THE GAME upon JUMPING TO THE BEACON! Maybe because of the "count" ?
	<weaponOverride count="4">
		<name>LIST_WEAPONS_ZOLTAN</name>
	</weaponOverride> 
	-->
	<crew>
		<crewMember type="zoltan" prop="0.50"/>
		<crewMember type="zoltan_peacekeeper" prop="0.50"/>	
	</crew>
</ship>

<event name="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_ACCEPT">
	<text>They come aboard and search your ship...</text>
	
	<choice req="DJMOD_HAS_RADIKAL_GEAR" lvl="0" max_lvl="0" hidden="true" blue="false">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event>
			<text>Luckily you had nothing to worry about, and after leaving your ship, without a word the Zoltans immediately cut comms to focus on a different ship. You wonder what could have happened. In any case this took a while, too long to do anything special on your ship.</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice req="DJMOD_HAS_RADIKAL_GEAR" lvl="1" hidden="true" blue="false">
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event>
			<text>Before long, they do find something. "Understand that without justification for this, which you may still provide, we will apply the necessary sanctions, which may be a fine or outright confiscation of the offending equipment. Both may be avoided if you willingly leave someone with us for interrogation."</text>
			<choice>
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event load="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_FINED"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="ZOLTAN_POLICECHECK_RK_FINED">
	<text>Maybe you forgot you were carrying RadiKal gear, or maybe you just didn't find a way to avoid the search. Regardless, they are now fining you for each piece!</text>
	
	<choice req="DJMOD_SUM_RADIKAL_EQUIPMENT" lvl="1" max_lvl="1" hidden="true">
		<text>Let them calculate your total fine.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"One illegal piece of gear, take this minimal fine as a warning. If you had any more "RadiKal" gear than that, we would have been forced to direct you to the local Police Station for processing."</text>
			<item_modify steal="true">
				<item type="scrap" min="-15" max="-15"/>
			</item_modify>

			<quest event="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<!-- From here, unlocks police station quest. MAKE THIS START AT ... one piece!? -->
	<choice req="DJMOD_SUM_RADIKAL_EQUIPMENT" lvl="2" max_lvl="2" hidden="true">
		<text>Let them calculate your total fine.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Two illegal pieces of gear. You should really know better than to give up ethics for power."
				Supposedly you can get some of your scrap back by surrendering your illegal gear at the Police Station, but somehow you doubt that. It might be worth it to pay them a visit regardless.
			</text>
			<item_modify steal="true">
				<item type="scrap" min="-30" max="-30"/>
			</item_modify>
			
			<quest event="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice req="DJMOD_SUM_RADIKAL_EQUIPMENT" lvl="3" max_lvl="3" hidden="true">
		<text>Let them calculate your total fine.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Three illegal pieces of gear... The federation really hires any random scum these days."
				Supposedly you can get some of your scrap back by surrendering your illegal gear at the Police Station, but somehow you doubt that. It might be worth it to pay them a visit regardless.
			</text>
			<!-- <event load="MORALITY_UPDATE_ZOLTAN_FIGHT"/> -->
			<item_modify steal="true">
				<item type="scrap" min="-45" max="-45"/>
			</item_modify>
			
			<quest event="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice req="DJMOD_SUM_RADIKAL_EQUIPMENT" lvl="4" hidden="true">
		<text>Let them calculate your total fine.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"AT LEAST FOUR illegal pieces of gear! What th-... I do not even wish to know. What a horrible person you must be. Luckily for you, this is the maximum fine stipulated in the applicable regulation. I suppose nobody foresaw that anyone would make themselves any more of a wretched menace to society than that."
				Supposedly you can get some of your scrap back by surrendering your illegal gear at the Police Station, but somehow you doubt that. It might be worth it to pay them a visit regardless.</text>
			<item_modify steal="true">
				<item type="scrap" min="-60" max="-60"/>
			</item_modify>
			
			<quest event="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK"/>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice req="LIST_CHECK_ANY_CREW" lvl="1" hidden="true" blue="true">
		<text>Give someone up for interrogation instead.</text>
		<event load="RK_INTERROGATED_CREW"/>
	</choice>

	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Surprise headshot that nosy lightbulb. (Risky)</text>
		<event>
			<text>Quickly but accurately aiming through the hardlight, you splatter the chief inspector with your blaster, right before taking cover for the explosion! 
			Very satisfying, and his badge will sell for some scrap... but can you deal with the rest of the squad?</text>
			<ship hostile="true"/>
			<!-- Can't remember why, but DO NOT MAKE IT MORE THAN 6 MAX -->
			<autoReward level="low">scrap_only</autoReward>
			<boarders min="4" max="6" class="zoltan_peacekeeper"/>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Pop them all!</text>
				<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="RK_INTERROGATED_CREW">
	<text>You come to an agreement where they keep one of your crew in custody so they can explain what you were doing in this sector. It's a lengthy process, you will certainly finish your mission (or die) before you see them again.</text>
	<removeCrew>			<!--No class argument means it's a random crewmember. Uniques immune if any non-uniques. -->
		<clone>false</clone>
		<text>Your crew cannot be cloned as they are not dead, though they might go insane shortly.</text>
	</removeCrew>
	
	<choice>
		<text>Continue...</text>
		<event/>
	</choice>
</event>

</FTL>

<!-- Player can raid to get gear or just loot. -->
<!-- <event name="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK" unique="true"> -->
<event name="ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK">
	<preventQuest/>
	<preventFleet/>
	<quest>
		<nebulaBeacon>false</nebulaBeacon>
		<aggressive>2</aggressive>			<!-- what does that even do? -->
	</quest>
	<beaconType id="map_icon_rk_policestation" global="true">
		<color r="94" g="255" b="94" a="1.0"/>
		<unvisitedTooltip>Where Zoltan Police holds confiscated RadiKal gear.</unvisitedTooltip>
	</beaconType>
	<text>You wonder how exactly the Zoltans set up a fortified police station in such an area undeterred, but it is proof of their determination.
		"Welcome captain. Since you found this place, you must be part of the special Federation corps attached to this regulation effort."
		
		Might be far from the truth, but you decide to roll with it.
		"What can we do for you?"
	</text>
	<ship load="SHIP_ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK" hostile="false"/>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Request supplies.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"We have seized quite a lot of supplies from this band of criminals, at great cost. But as Federation you are our ally in this operation. Help yourself, within the limits of the Alliance Supply and Logistics Act of course."</text>
			<autoReward level="MED">stuff</autoReward>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Request RadiKal gear.</text>
		<event>
			<text>After some brief icebreaker chitchat which the officer almost seems to enjoy, you take your shot asking for a free piece. What passes for his facial expression changes that instant.
				"Surely you must be confused. This is labeled and sorted trial evidence, in the form of illegal weaponry which is unsafe for use, unethical and generally a threat to law and order. Thanks for stopping by, I have work to do now."
			</text>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Feign surprise.</text>
				<event>
					<text>You expected this. "Oh? We weren't informed. Sorry for asking, keep up the good work." 
						The Zoltan throws you a suspicious look, but he's too busy dealing with the paperwork to investigate. You're out without a hitch but with nothing to show for it.
					</text>
					
					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>Meh.</text>
						<event/>
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>"We can do this the hard way instead..."</text>
				<event>
					<text>Now certain that you're not, in fact, here to help at all, the Zoltan rings the alarm and you rush back to your ship. The fight is breaking out within range of the station's defense turrets!</text>
					<ship hostile="true"/>
					<environment type="PDS" target="player"/>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>

<ship name="SHIP_ZOLTAN_POLICESTATION_RK" auto_blueprint="MU_ZOLTAN_STATION">
	<destroyed>
		<text>The police station breaks apart, its confiscated illegal contents and extensive array of administrative backups reduced to mere scrap for you to take.</text>
		<autoReward level="HIGH">standard</autoReward>
	</destroyed>
	<deadCrew>
		<text>Having killed the crew, you manage to snatch some supplies and a labeled crate before the turrets tear your ship apart.</text>
		<autoReward level="HIGH">standard</autoReward>
		<choice hidden="true">
			<text>Open it.</text>
			<event>
				<text>As the label suggested, it's a RadiKal augment! Bureaucracy has its benefits.</text>
				<augment name="GIFTLIST_AUGMENT_RADIKAL"/>
			</event>
		</choice>
	</deadCrew>
	<crew>
		<crewMember type="zoltan" prop="0.50"/>
		<crewMember type="zoltan_peacekeeper" prop="0.50"/>	
	</crew>
</ship>

<!-- 
*********************************************************************************************************
*********************************************************************************************************
ZOLTAN POLICE QUESTS END
*********************************************************************************************************
*********************************************************************************************************
-->

<!-- 
RK ships under attack, giving subfaction-theme-fitting gear when saved, or RK gear when crewkilled. 
_LASERS version updated 5.5.1, re-copypaste the others completely, based on this one.
-->
<FTL>
<event name="THIEVES_RK_LASERS">
	<text>It appears a heavily damaged laser-wielding RadiKal ship is under attack by an Argeonn smuggler, certainly to steal their special tech. They are on their last legs but their trajectory forces them to pass you by for a slim chance at escaping.</text>
	<ship load="SHIP_SMUGGLER_RK_LASERS" hostile="false"/>
	
	<choice>
		<text>Rescue the RadiKals.</text>
		<event>
			<text>You give the smuggler ship no choice but to fight you as you take position in their way.</text> 
			<ship hostile="true"/>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event load="COMBAT_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true" req="weapons" lvl="5">
		<text>(Upg. Weapons) Claim the prey for yourself.</text>
		<event>
			<text>"Woh hoh hoh, hey, wait, that's our-" They quickly change their mind as the rest of the crew pressures them. "You know what, screw this, have fun with you ill-gotten goods." Quite ironic, coming from a smuggler. The surviving RadiKals are easily dealt with.</text>
			<autoReward level="LOW">standard</autoReward>
			
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Search the ship a little more.</text>
				<event>
					<text>There was a functional RadiKal augment in the cargo! Must be what the smugglers were after.</text>
					<augment name="GIFTLIST_AUGMENT_RADIKAL"/>

					<choice hidden="true">
						<text>I guess we're the thieves now.</text>
						
						<event load="REPUTATION_DECREASE_SMUGGLING"/>
						<!-- <event load="REPUTATION_UPDATE_SMUGGLING_FREE"/> -->
					</choice>
				</event>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>

	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Stay back and watch how this unfolds.</text>
		<event>
			<text>The RadiKal ship puts up a decent but hopeless fight and soon stops showing signs of life. The pirates briefly do whatever they went in there for, then re-open comms with you. "Thank you for not interfering my good sir. Imagine how much easier business would be if we had more cowa- I mean nice bystanders like you around? Here's some fuel for your exemplary behavior, and we're off to celebrate!" You scoop up the reward and briefly wonder what could have put them in such a good mood.</text>
			<autoReward level="LOW">fuel_only</autoReward>
			<!-- <item_modify>
				<item type="scrap" min="5" max="10"/>
			</item_modify> -->
			<instantEscape/>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event load="REPUTATION_UPDATE_SMUGGLING_FREE"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Ignore them.</text>
		<event>
			<text>You leave the ships to their fight and think about what to do next.</text>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Do something onboard the ship.</text>
				<event load="STORAGE_CHECK"/>
			</choice>
			<choice>
				<text>Do nothing.</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>
<!-- TODO: TEST: if no work, move to events_ships & RETEST. -->
<ship name="SHIP_SMUGGLER_RK_LASERS" auto_blueprint="LIST_SHIPS_SMUGGLERS">
	<!-- <surrender min="999" max="999" load="SURRENDER_PIRATE"/> this is an instant surrender, which can be used for any event actually, like Guard ASB call. -->
	<!-- <surrender min="1" max="2" load="CRYSTAL_BOSS_SURRENDER"/> REF from spare crystal queen unlock quest. -->
	<!-- <surrender chance="0.4" min="2" max="3" load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD_SURR"/> IT NEVER CONTINUES THE QUESTLINE, JUST GIVES SURR REWARD -->
	<!-- <surrender min="1" max="3" load="SHIP_SMUGGLER_RK_LASERS_SURRENDER"/> This name format doesn't work either. -->
	
	<destroyed load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD"/>
	<deadCrew load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD_CREWKILL"/>
</ship>

<event name="SHIP_SMUGGLER_RK_LASERS_SURRENDER">
	<text load="TEXT_SURRENDER_PIRATE"/>
	<choice>
		<text>Accept their surrender.</text>
		<event>
			<ship hostile="false"/>
			<autoReward level="LOW">stuff</autoReward>
			
			<choice>
				<text>Go and check on their would-be prey.</text>
				<event load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD"/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	<choice>
		<text load="GENERIC_SURRENDER_CHOICE_NOMERCY"/>
		<event/>
	</choice>
</event>
<event name="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD">
	<text>"Without you we were toast. Have this as thanks."</text>
	<autoReward level="LOW">standard</autoReward>
	
	<choice>
		<text>What did they want from you?</text>
		<event load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_END"/>
	</choice>
</event>
<event name="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_REWARD_CREWKILL">
	<text>"Without you we were toast. Have this as thanks."</text>
	<autoReward level="MED">standard</autoReward>
	
	<choice>
		<text>What did they want from you?</text>
		<event load="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_END"/>
	</choice>
</event>

<event name="THIEVES_RK_LASERS_END">
	<text>"The usual, local tech. Surely you understand that we can't just give it to you either."
		A voice in the back of your head tells you that you should have killed them then... but you keep your greed in check and dismiss the intrusive thoughts.
		
		"However we can provide you one non-RadiKal laser weapon that fits the style of an RK subfaction, that would only be fair. Which one is it?"
	</text> 
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Bam</text>
		<event>
			<text>They transfer the weapon and wish you safe travels.</text> 
			<weapon name="GIFTLIST_FITTING_LASER_BAM"/>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Punk</text>
		<event>
			<text>They transfer the weapon and wish you safe travels.</text> 
			<weapon name="GIFTLIST_FITTING_LASER_PUNK"/>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
	
	<choice hidden="true">
		<text>Scorch</text>
		<event>
			<text>They transfer the weapon and wish you safe travels.</text> 
			<weapon name="GIFTLIST_FITTING_LASER_SCORCH"/>
			<choice hidden="true">
				<text>Continue...</text>
				<event/>
			</choice>
		</event>
	</choice>
</event>

</FTL>

